 or incorrect. By inspecting the ConfigMap, they can verify if the credentials are properly configured. If the ConfigMap is missing the password, the Secret would be the next target. But first, let\'s get the details from the ConfigMap.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl describe configmap rate-mongodb -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-991476215098e4b9', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 420, 'prompt_tokens': 4862, 'total_tokens': 5282, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb31-79bb-7eb0-a7b0-e4c27ed2d3c0-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl describe configmap rate-mongodb -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-991476215098e4b9', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4862, 'output_tokens': 420, 'total_tokens': 5282}), ToolMessage(content='Command Rejected: Error executing kubectl command:\nError from server (NotFound): configmaps "rate-mongodb" not found\n', id='f9d284e0-08d5-4125-8a50-c826a79240fc', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-991476215098e4b9'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='59f1ab8b-8cb7-40c0-8fb9-279df27668db'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose why the "rate" service is failing. The logs showed an authorization error when connecting to MongoDB. The previous attempt to get the ConfigMap "rate-mongodb" didn\'t work because it doesn\'t exist. So, maybe the credentials are stored in a Secret instead.\n\nIn K