\nAfter identifying the correct secret name, the next step would be to describe that secret to get the username and password. But first, listing all secrets is crucial to find the right one. This approach ensures that the user doesn\'t miss the secret because of a wrong name assumption.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The "mongodb-rate" secret was not found, so I need to list all secrets in the namespace to identify the correct one containing the MongoDB credentials for the "rate" service. The command `kubectl get secrets -n hotel-reservation` will reveal all available secrets, allowing me to check for a secret related to "rate-db" or "mongodb-rate".  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd", "arguments": {"command": "kubectl get secrets -n hotel-reservation"}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 386, 'prompt_tokens': 4558, 'total_tokens': 4944, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb32-0a30-7b63-b3a1-2fa36914842b-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4558, 'output_tokens': 386, 'total_tokens': 4944}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='6d7d4421-3c12-4ac9-a3e8-c785cb38c201'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s try to figure out why the "rate" service is failing. From the logs, there\'s an authorization error when connecting to the MongoDB database. The error message says "not authorized on rate-db to execute command". So the issue is likely with the credentials used by the "rate" service to access the MongoDB database.\n\nEarlier attempts to check ConfigMaps and Secrets like "rate-mongodb" and "rate-db-secret" didn\'t work because those resources weren\'t found. Now, I need to list all the Secrets in the "hotel-reservation" namespace to find the correct one that contains the credentials for the MongoDB database. The command `kubectl get secrets -n hotel-reservation` should show all available Secrets. Once I have the list, I can look for a Secret that might be related to the "rate" service or the MongoDB database, such as "mongodb-rate" or "rate-db". \n\nWait, the user tried "mongodb-rate" and it wasn\'t found. Maybe the Secret has a different name. Perhaps it\'s named something like "mongodb-rate-secret" or "rate-db-credentials". After listing all Secrets, I can check each one\'s description to find the right credentials. Once identified, I can retrieve the username and password from the Secret to verify if they\'re correct and match the MongoDB database\'s requirements. This will help determine if the credentials are the root cause of the authorization error.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get secrets -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ba30acecc3d693d9', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 323, 'prompt_tokens': 5579, 'total_tokens': 5902, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb32-1c5e-74c3-8e38-3a97d2eb848a-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get secrets -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-ba30acecc3d693d9', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5579, 'output_tokens': 323, 'total_tokens': 5902}), ToolMessage(content='', id='4a740767-2514-471e-9c10-da17b1f84173', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-ba30acecc3d693d9'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='cc1627a5-fda4-4da9-9440-abf60a51f3a1')]]
