secret") have failed. This indicates the "rate" service lacks proper credentials to authenticate with the "rate-db" MongoDB instance, causing the "not authorized" error in the logs. The root cause is the absence of the required Secret for MongoDB authentication.  \n\n{"ans": "The \'rate\' service is failing due to a missing MongoDB authentication Secret. The deployment YAML for \'rate\' does not reference any Secret or ConfigMap containing the MongoDB credentials (username/password) required to connect to \'rate-db\'. The error \'not authorized on rate-db to execute command\' confirms the absence of valid credentials. The root cause is the missing Secret (e.g., \'mongodb-rate-secret\') that should provide the necessary authentication details for the \'rate\' service to access the MongoDB database."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=705, prompt_tokens=6277, total_tokens=6982, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb32-bc92-7ac1-ac6e-5d9c4e32c73a-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6277, 'output_tokens': 705, 'total_tokens': 6982}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='22add1cd-90d4-4a35-8565-344cd2849f66')]]
